      ],
      "comment": "Mamere: Narcissus's Waltz",
      "content": "At a tea party in Nasha Town, Sandrone invites Mamere and Seymour, then Mary-Ann and Ann, to become a new 'family'. Mamere paints a family portrait afterwards.\n\nSeymour concludes logically that Sandrone is a different person from his master Mary-Ann despite the likeness.",
